38
00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:40.789
Tim Nunamaker: maybe I have a server, I want to get some data into it, but I need some standard way of going out and collecting data from data sources that are not under my direct control. The collection profile, I'll explain kind of how it works. That's a separate protocol for a standard way to collect data.

39
00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:53.079
Tim Nunamaker: All data connectors implement the collection profile, and the key piece of a data connector

40
00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:58.980
Tim Nunamaker: That makes it compatible with PDPP and with the collection profile.

41
00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:03.760
Tim Nunamaker: is… it's manifest. And so this manifest is…

42
00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:13.840
Tim Nunamaker: basically an extension of the source declaration in the PDPP standard, and so this is where you're going to see what is the shape of the data.

43
00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:18.289
Tim Nunamaker: What is the identifier for this, connector?

44
00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:21.420
Tim Nunamaker: And what version is it on?

45
00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:28.900
Tim Nunamaker: You'll also see… For this piece of code that implements data collection for this data source.

46
00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:42.180
Tim Nunamaker: what exactly is required, from the runtime that it's executing within. So if it needs to access the internet, things like that, it can declare, sort of runtime requirements.

47
00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:49.329
